      "description": "Watch AZ Alkmaar vs ADO Den Haag highlights and goals from Eredivisie on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 8, 2026. The Eredivisie clash between AZ Alkmaar and ADO Den Haag was a tactical battle defined by patience and second-half precision. Both sides entered the pitch looking to assert dominance, but it was a game of fine margins that ultimately decided the outcome. VAR Drama and Early Resistance Taking place on August 8, 2026, the match began with high energy as AZ Alkmaar pushed for an early advantage. The defining moment of the first half arrived in the 24th minute when the home side thought they had broken the deadlock. However, after a lengthy VAR review, the referee revoked the goal due to a foul committed earlier in the build-up. This decision breathed new life into ADO Den Haag , who remained disciplined despite constant pressure from the hosts' corner routines. AZ continued to search for an opener, with Mexx Meerdink even attempting an audacious bicycle kick early in the second half that unfortunately flew wide. It became clear that fresh legs were needed to break the stalemate, leading to a quadruple substitution by the home side in the 57th minute. Clinical Finishing Seals the Win The tactical changes paid immediate dividends. In the 61st minute, Ro-Zangelo Daal capitalized on a defensive error by Pascal Mulder , clinical finishing with his right foot to give AZ Alkmaar the lead. The momentum stayed firmly with the hosts, and just seven minutes later, the lead was doubled. A brilliant sequence involving Daal and Kees Smit set up Calvin Stengs for a simple tap-in, effectively ending the contest. ADO Den Haag struggled to create clear-cut chances in response, though Yannick Eduardo missed a header late in stoppage time that could have provided a consolation. Ultimately, AZ Alkmaar controlled 53% of possession and secured a deserved victory, showcasing their superior quality when it mattered most."
